<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">5 February in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 5 February, from 2 BCE to 1971.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/roman-senate" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/roman-senate.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">2 BCE <span class="tih-ago">2,027 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Senate grants Augustus the title pater patriae</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-senate">Roman Senate</a> gave Augustus the title pater patriae, 'father of the country', which was then inscribed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>, including in the Senate chambers in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-forum">Forum Romanum</a>. Under the Republic it had been awarded only to Camillus and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cicero">Cicero</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-senate">Roman Senate</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">62 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,964 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Earthquake strikes Pompeii and Herculaneum</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A strong earthquake badly damaged towns around the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bay-of-naples">Bay of Naples</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pompeii">Pompeii</a> was still being repaired seventeen years later when Vesuvius buried it in 79.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/756">756 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,270 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">An Lushan proclaims himself emperor of Yan at Luoyang</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The rebel Tang general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/an-lushan">An Lushan</a> declared himself emperor at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luoyang">Luoyang</a> on the Lunar New Year, founding the state of Yan, and named Zhang Tongru and the surrendered Tang official Daxi Xun his chancellors. Yan collapsed in 763.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/an-lushan">An Lushan</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1597">1597 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">429 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Twenty-six Christians crucified at Nagasaki</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the orders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a>, six Franciscan missionaries, Japanese <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuits</a> and lay converts were crucified on a hill at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagasaki">Nagasaki</a>. They are honoured as the Twenty-Six Martyrs of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nagasaki">Nagasaki</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuits</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1783">1783 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">243 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Calabrian earthquakes begin in southern Italy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The first of five major shocks struck <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/calabria">Calabria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a>, beginning a sequence that lasted weeks. Around 30,000 to 50,000 people died, and the disaster prompted early scientific study of earthquakes.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1852">1852 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">174 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">New Hermitage museum opens to the public in St Petersburg</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Nicholas I opened the purpose-built New Hermitage to display the imperial art collections. The Hermitage is now one of the largest museums in the world.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1900">1900 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">126 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Britain and the United States sign the first Hay-Pauncefote Treaty</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The agreement gave the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> the right to build a canal across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-america">Central America</a>. Rejected by the Senate, it was renegotiated in 1901, opening the way for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/panama-canal">Panama Canal</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1924">1924 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">102 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">BBC broadcasts the Greenwich time signal for the first time</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The six short 'pips', generated by the Royal Observatory at Greenwich, were broadcast to mark the hour. The signal is still heard on BBC radio today.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1971">1971 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">55 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Apollo 14 lands at Fra Mauro</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Alan Shepard and Edgar Mitchell landed in the lunar highlands, the target of the aborted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apollo">Apollo</a> 13. Shepard, America's first astronaut in space, became the fifth person to walk on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhu">Moon</a>.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 5 February <span class="n">3</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/rene-of-chalon"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/rene-of-chalon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">René of Chalon</span><span class="tp">1519–1544</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/john-boyd-dunlop"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/john-boyd-dunlop.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">John Boyd Dunlop</span><span class="tp">1840–1921</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/andreas-papandreou"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/andreas-papandreou.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Andreas Papandreou</span><span class="tp">1919–1996</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
